WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.100
-Okay, everybody. Welcome, welcome, welcome

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.901
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.901 --> 00:00:05.501
You're here. You're watching.

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:06.934
Happy Friday.

00:00:06.934 --> 00:00:08.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:10.434
Well, guys, everyone's talking about this today.

00:00:10.434 --> 00:00:13.133
"John Wick: Chapter 4" hit theaters.

00:00:13.133 --> 00:00:15.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.367 --> 00:00:18.000
He's angry. [ Cymbal clangs ]

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.133
He's out for revenge. [ Cymbal clangs ]

00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:22.467
He's promising death and destruction.

00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:24.234
[ Cymbal clangs ] Oh. Sorry. I read that wrong.

00:00:24.234 --> 00:00:25.334
I was talking about Donald Trump.

00:00:25.334 --> 00:00:27.200
Sorry about that. I apologize. I apologize.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.734
Sorry. Sorry.

00:00:28.734 --> 00:00:31.067
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:32.834
I don't know if you guys saw this,

00:00:32.834 --> 00:00:34.234
but late last night

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.367
Trump threatened the Manhattan District Attorney

00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:39.167
saying that if he's charged "death and destruction"

00:00:39.167 --> 00:00:40.734
could follow.

00:00:40.734 --> 00:00:43.100
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.234
America said, "No way.

00:00:44.234 --> 00:00:45.868
That's only gonna happen if they ban TikTok."

00:00:45.868 --> 00:00:47.400
That's the only way that's gonna happen.

00:00:48.868 --> 00:00:50.767
Yep. Death and destruction.

00:00:50.767 --> 00:00:52.300
It sounds bad, but he makes the same threat

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.300
when Little Caesar's forgets his Crazy Bread.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.701
So, it's like, "Death and destruction." Okay.

00:00:56.701 --> 00:00:59.067
[ Laughter ] That's right.

00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:02.367
It's day four of Trump indictment watch, 2023.

00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:04.868
Still nothing.

00:01:04.868 --> 00:01:08.501
It feels like one of those viral videos that says "wait for it"

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:09.834
and two minutes you're like, "I don't know

00:01:09.834 --> 00:01:12.234
if I'm gonna wait anymore."

00:01:12.234 --> 00:01:14.234
Four days. Four days.

00:01:14.234 --> 00:01:16.300
We're basically -- We basically all went into labor

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:18.601
and four days later we're still chewing on ice chips.

00:01:18.601 --> 00:01:21.200
You know what I'm saying? [ Laughter ]

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.000
Meanwhile, I heard that Melania Trump

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.701
is still angry at her husband

00:01:24.701 --> 00:01:26.501
over the Stormy Daniels scandal

00:01:26.501 --> 00:01:30.000
and doesn't sympathize with him for facing charges.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.901
That's shocking given how warm and affectionate

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:33.367
she and Donald are in public.

00:01:33.367 --> 00:01:35.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.601 --> 00:01:37.801
You can tell Melania's mad 'cause the last three nights

00:01:37.801 --> 00:01:40.133
Donald's been sleeping on the golden futon.

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:42.334
[ Laughter ] Well, get this.

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:45.267
Florida Governor Ron DeSantis said that he would not accept

00:01:45.267 --> 00:01:47.601
an offer to be Trump's running mate.

00:01:47.601 --> 00:01:49.767
That's shocking given how warm and affectionate

00:01:49.767 --> 00:01:51.300
he and Donald are in public.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:52.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.701 --> 00:01:54.734
I think it's a good decision 'cause Don and Ron

00:01:54.734 --> 00:01:56.601
doesn't sound like the leaders of the free world.

00:01:56.601 --> 00:01:58.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:00.234
Sound like twin brothers on TikTok.

00:02:00.234 --> 00:02:02.133
-Who painted the "Mona Lisa"?

00:02:02.133 --> 00:02:03.367
Mona Lisa.

00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:04.801
-Yeah.

00:02:04.801 --> 00:02:05.901
-"Da Vinki"?

00:02:05.901 --> 00:02:08.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.033 --> 00:02:09.234
-"Vinki"?

00:02:09.234 --> 00:02:12.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:13.467
I saw...

00:02:13.467 --> 00:02:16.234
I saw that President Biden was in Ottawa today,

00:02:16.234 --> 00:02:18.601
where he made a big speech to Canada's parliament.

00:02:18.601 --> 00:02:21.767
Here he is with Canada's Prime Minister Justin Trudeau.

00:02:21.767 --> 00:02:23.868
Wow. Look at those guys.

00:02:23.868 --> 00:02:25.767
They look like Yoda and Baby Yoda.

00:02:25.767 --> 00:02:30.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.334 --> 00:02:32.667
They look Alfred the butler and Bruce Wayne.

00:02:32.667 --> 00:02:35.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.167 --> 00:02:36.767
They look like the old man from "Up"

00:02:36.767 --> 00:02:37.968
and the kid reunited.

00:02:37.968 --> 00:02:42.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.033 --> 00:02:44.100
They look like the guy who did it on "Scooby Doo"

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:45.701
and the guy who did it on "Dateline."

00:02:45.701 --> 00:02:48.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:51.267
They look like Logan and Roman Roy's stunt doubles

00:02:51.267 --> 00:02:53.601
on "Succession." [ Laughter ]

00:02:53.601 --> 00:02:55.133
They look like an American remake

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:56.801
of "The Banshees of Inisherin."

00:02:56.801 --> 00:02:59.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:01.100
They looked like a Planet Fitness customer

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:02.634
and an Equinox customer.

00:03:02.634 --> 00:03:06.200
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.467
[ Applause ]

00:03:08.467 --> 00:03:10.501
[ Sighs ]

00:03:10.501 --> 00:03:13.100
One more. One more. One more.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:14.801
Finally, they look like

00:03:14.801 --> 00:03:17.100
Doc Brown and Marty McFly at a business luncheon.

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:19.234
There you go. That's it. That's it. That's what they look like.

00:03:19.234 --> 00:03:23.767
♪♪

00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:26.601
Speaking of Biden, I read that he is frustrated

00:03:26.601 --> 00:03:28.300
with Vice President Kamala Harris

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:32.000
for not constantly rising to the occasion.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.300
Kamala was like, "Sorry.

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:35.267
Unlike you, I can't take a little blue pill for that."

00:03:35.267 --> 00:03:38.767
[ Laughter, groaning ]

00:03:42.968 --> 00:03:44.267
"Da Vinki"?

00:03:45.501 --> 00:03:47.267
Yep. Biden said it's tough having to

00:03:47.267 --> 00:03:48.868
worry about your VP all the time.

00:03:48.868 --> 00:03:51.167
Then Obama was like, "Oh, you get used to it, Joe."

00:03:51.167 --> 00:03:53.534
[ Laughter ] That's right.

00:03:53.534 --> 00:03:55.000
Biden's frustrated with Kamala

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:58.367
'cause apparently she isn't taking anything off his plate.

00:03:58.367 --> 00:04:00.634
Which is the opposite of Trump, who was always frustrated

00:04:00.634 --> 00:04:02.400
when Pence took something off his plate.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.100
"Did I say you could have that fry?"

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:07.367
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.367 --> 00:04:08.868
Some more news from the White House.

00:04:08.868 --> 00:04:10.968
The Biden administration is rolling out new rules

00:04:10.968 --> 00:04:14.734
to require more efficient window air conditions.

00:04:14.734 --> 00:04:16.734
Yep. And instead of low, medium, and high,

00:04:16.734 --> 00:04:18.767
the controls will now be more accurately labeled as

00:04:18.767 --> 00:04:21.501
low, same but louder, and same but much louder.

00:04:21.501 --> 00:04:23.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.601
First gas ovens, and now air conditioners.

00:04:25.601 --> 00:04:26.834
It's been a busy few months

00:04:26.834 --> 00:04:29.000
for Biden's Secretary of Homeland Appliances.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:30.767
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.767 --> 00:04:32.868
And, finally, I saw that Apple is gonna spend

00:04:32.868 --> 00:04:34.367
$1 billion a year

00:04:34.367 --> 00:04:37.234
to make movies that will be released in theaters.

00:04:37.234 --> 00:04:38.400
It'll be fun.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:40.000
Instead of trailers, every movie will start

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.667
with 30 minutes of "Terms and Conditions."

00:04:41.667 --> 00:04:43.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.501 --> 00:04:44.968
You'll know you're watching an Apple movie

00:04:44.968 --> 00:04:46.868
when all the screens are cracked.

00:04:46.868 --> 00:04:48.467
We have a great show.

00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:49.567
Let's go write some thank you notes.

00:04:49.567 --> 00:04:51.234
Come with me now. Yeah.

00:04:51.234 --> 00:04:59.467
♪♪

00:04:59.467 --> 00:05:02.067
Oh, what a show we have for you tonight.

00:05:02.067 --> 00:05:04.634
One of my favorites, he's an Emmy-nominated actor

00:05:04.634 --> 00:05:07.434
who stars as Roman Roy in "Succession."

00:05:07.434 --> 00:05:08.968
The fourth and final season

00:05:08.968 --> 00:05:12.200
premieres this Sunday on HBO and HBO Max.

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:14.367
Kieran Culkin is here tonight!

00:05:14.367 --> 00:05:18.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:18.667 --> 00:05:22.334
He stars in the show "Power Book II: Ghost,"

00:05:22.334 --> 00:05:24.601
which airs Fridays on Starz.

00:05:24.601 --> 00:05:26.968
Method Man is joining us!

00:05:26.968 --> 00:05:30.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:30.033 --> 00:05:32.033
And we've got great music tonight.

00:05:32.033 --> 00:05:34.300
He is a global pop music icon

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.033
who you know from BTS.

00:05:36.033 --> 00:05:38.534
His new EP "Face" is out now,

00:05:38.534 --> 00:05:40.868
and tonight he's performing "Like Crazy,"

00:05:40.868 --> 00:05:44.033
which is the number-one song on iTunes right now.

00:05:44.033 --> 00:05:46.901
Jimin is here tonight!

00:05:46.901 --> 00:05:48.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:48.033 --> 00:05:49.534
Jimin!

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:54.200
Today's Friday, and that's usually when I catch up

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:55.300
on some personal stuff.

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:57.400
I check my inbox, return some e-mails,

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:59.300
and of course I send out thank you notes.

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:01.834
And I was just... [ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:01.834 --> 00:06:03.634
...running a bit behind.

00:06:03.634 --> 00:06:05.334
I thought today, if you guys wouldn't mind,

00:06:05.334 --> 00:06:07.634
I'd just like to write out my weekly thank you notes.

00:06:07.634 --> 00:06:08.901
[ Laughter ]

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:10.234
Is that cool?

00:06:10.234 --> 00:06:11.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:12.601
Thank you very much.

00:06:12.601 --> 00:06:13.701
James, can I get some

00:06:13.701 --> 00:06:15.334
thank-you-note-writing music, please?

00:06:15.334 --> 00:06:16.501
Thanks so much.

00:06:16.501 --> 00:06:19.767
[ Somber music playing ]

00:06:19.767 --> 00:06:21.601
He forgot his tie again.

00:06:21.601 --> 00:06:23.868
♪♪

00:06:27.934 --> 00:06:29.501
♪♪

00:06:29.501 --> 00:06:32.434
Thank you, Trump indictment protests,

00:06:32.434 --> 00:06:35.000
for looking like one guy decided to dry his beach towels

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.400
in front of Trump Tower.

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:37.734
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:06:37.734 --> 00:06:39.100
Four guys.

00:06:44.033 --> 00:06:45.300
♪♪

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:48.534
Thank you, TikTok stars marching in Washington,

00:06:48.534 --> 00:06:49.834
for being the first time

00:06:49.834 --> 00:06:52.501
a protest chant ends with "Sheesh!"

00:06:52.501 --> 00:06:56.968
[ Laughter ]

00:06:58.601 --> 00:07:00.100
♪♪

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:03.701
Thank you, Spring, for being when the flowers bloom,

00:07:03.701 --> 00:07:06.634
the birds sing, and the bears come out of hibernation

00:07:06.634 --> 00:07:08.200
to look for cocaine.

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:11.634
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:07:15.934 --> 00:07:17.701
♪♪

00:07:17.701 --> 00:07:20.067
Thank you, allergy medicine,

00:07:20.067 --> 00:07:22.767
for being the reason I don't sneeze through my kid's recital

00:07:22.767 --> 00:07:24.567
but snore through it instead.

00:07:24.567 --> 00:07:26.667
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:07:31.367 --> 00:07:32.501
[ Chuckles ]

00:07:32.501 --> 00:07:33.734
♪♪

00:07:33.734 --> 00:07:35.968
Thank you, barbed wire,

00:07:35.968 --> 00:07:38.534
for not going by your other name, "Evil Slinky."

00:07:38.534 --> 00:07:42.200
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:44.234
[ Rim shot ]

00:07:44.234 --> 00:07:46.334
That's a jab. Come on, man.

00:07:46.334 --> 00:07:48.167
That's a jab.

00:07:49.901 --> 00:07:51.234
♪♪

00:07:51.234 --> 00:07:54.133
Thank you, "John Wick 4," "Shazam 2,"

00:07:54.133 --> 00:07:56.033
"Scream VI," and "Creed III,"

00:07:56.033 --> 00:07:58.267
for sounding more like a Bingo card

00:07:58.267 --> 00:07:59.701
than a weekend at the movies.

00:07:59.701 --> 00:08:02.934
[ Laughter, applause ] Oh, I got it! Bingo!

00:08:07.601 --> 00:08:08.901
♪♪

00:08:08.901 --> 00:08:10.634
Thank you, bird houses,

00:08:10.634 --> 00:08:12.701
for being nature's Airbnbs.

00:08:12.701 --> 00:08:14.634
There you have it, everybody. Those are my thank you notes.

